7.Based on the ExecuteCommand() return value and the output returned from the mediapipelinetests application, TM return SUCCESS/FAILURE status.', '1. Verify the API call is success
Checkpoint 2. Verify that the output returned from mediapipelinetests contains the strings "Failures: 0" and "Errors: 0", or "failed: 0"', '901d97cd-0bfa-48c8-a30d-16705186059e', '2026-06-16 10:44:09.881134', '2026-06-16 10:44:09.881134');
