6.Verify the output from the execute command and check if the strings "Failures: 0" and "Errors: 0", or "failed: 0" exists in the returned output
7.Based on the ExecuteCommand() return value and the output returned from the mediapipelinetests application, TM return SUCCESS/FAILURE status.', 'pipeline should ply with normal playback rate  after seeking to audioStart point from audioEnd point where audio underrun has occurred', 'ee17d1b2-f9c4-4889-919e-9ccb30d71d4e', '2026-06-16 10:44:12.161916', '2026-06-16 10:44:12.161917');
