7.Based on the ExecuteCommand() return value and the output returned from the mediapipelinetests application, TM return SUCCESS/FAILURE status.', 'Checkpoint 1. Verify the API call is success
Checkpoint 2. Verify that the output returned from mediapipelinetests contains the strings "Failures: 0" and "Errors: 0" or it contains the string "failed: 0"', '8cc3a472-5851-4b11-ab82-ce8ed00fa5e7', '2026-06-16 10:44:06.446626', '2026-06-16 10:44:06.446628');
